sequenceDiagram
    participant R1 as Request 1
    participant R2 as Request 2
    participant DB as PostgreSQL (SSI)

    R1->>DB: BEGIN SERIALIZABLE
    R2->>DB: BEGIN SERIALIZABLE

    R1->>DB: SELECT available_seats (= 1)
    R2->>DB: SELECT available_seats (= 1)

    R1->>DB: UPDATE available_seats = 0
    R1->>DB: COMMIT

    R2->>DB: UPDATE available_seats = 0
    DB-->>R2: ERROR 40001: serialization failure
    Note over R2,DB: SSI detects R2 read a value<br/>that R1 has now changed
    Note over R2: Retry (up to 3 times)<br/>then NoSeatsAvailableException
